{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"73999d11-8555-4341-b0cf-62410abab56b","title":"The normal distribution and the 68-95-99.7 rule"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73999d11-8555-4341-b0cf-62410abab56b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A normal distribution is symmetric and bell-shaped. Its mean sets the center, while its standard deviation measures spread.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"The normal distribution"},{"op":"equation","id":"parameters","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\mu=\\text{mean},\\qquad \\sigma=\\text{standard deviation}"},{"op":"diagram","id":"bell","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.08,0.55],[0.92,0.55]],"stroke":"solid"},{"kind":"smooth","points":[[0.15,0.549],[0.2,0.545],[0.3,0.492],[0.35,0.41],[0.4,0.289],[0.5,0.12],[0.6,0.289],[0.65,0.41],[0.7,0.492],[0.8,0.545],[0.85,0.549]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"symmetric normal density centered at the mean"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.5,0.12],[0.5,0.55]],"stroke":"dashed","label":"μ"}],"tension":0.55}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73999d11-8555-4341-b0cf-62410abab56b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"About 68 percent of the distribution lies within one standard deviation of the mean. Percentages describe area under the curve, not height.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"oneband","canvas_id":"bell","from":[0.4,0.64],"to":[0.6,0.64],"stroke":"solid","label":"68%"},{"op":"equation","id":"onerange","anchor":{"el":"parameters","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\mu-\\sigma\\leq X\\leq\\mu+\\sigma\\quad\\approx68\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"73999d11-8555-4341-b0cf-62410abab56b","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73999d11-8555-4341-b0cf-62410abab56b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Widening the interval to two standard deviations captures about 95 percent, leaving about 5 percent split equally between the two tails.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"twoband","canvas_id":"bell","from":[0.3,0.75],"to":[0.7,0.75],"stroke":"solid","label":"95%"},{"op":"equation","id":"tworange","anchor":{"el":"onerange","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(\\mu-2\\sigma\\leq X\\leq\\mu+2\\sigma)\\approx95\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73999d11-8555-4341-b0cf-62410abab56b","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Within three standard deviations lies about 99.7 percent. This rule applies to normal distributions, not automatically to every dataset.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"threeband","canvas_id":"bell","from":[0.2,0.86],"to":[0.8,0.86],"stroke":"solid","label":"99.7%"},{"op":"equation","id":"threerange","anchor":{"el":"tworange","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\mu-3\\sigma\\leq X\\leq\\mu+3\\sigma\\quad\\approx99.7\\%"},{"op":"text","id":"caution","anchor":{"el":"threerange","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Use for normal or approximately normal data."}],"checkpoint":null}}
